  "body": "﻿## What changed\n\n- New library machine `assets/machines/ooznest-workbee-1000x1500.mch`, \"Ooznest WorkBee 1000x1500 (Estlcam)\", kind `mill`:\n  - X 1200 mm, Y 770 mm, Z 88 mm travel (written `-L..L`).\n  - X and Y feed and rapid 2500 mm/min. Z rates are not stated.\n  - Spindle power 2.2 kW (the WorkBee's owner). No rpm range is stated.\n  - No coolant, no tool count, no `controller.post`.\n- The machine picker row and the bundled include line in `crates/app/src/posting_files.rs`.\n- The decision record `docs/decisions/3038-workbee-estlcam.md` with all sources.\n\n## Work area: the smaller value on each axis\n\nThe maintainer decided this on 2026-11-23. The WorkBee's owner (MisterMaker) gave 1200 x 800 mm (X x Y). Ooznest's public page for the 1000x1500 frame gives 1270 x 770 mm and Z 88 mm.\n- X 1200 mm: the owner's figure, inside the published 1270.\n- Y 770 mm: the published figure. The owner's 800 is more than it.\n- Z 88 mm: the published figure. The owner has not stated Z.\n\nA smaller travel can refuse a program that the machine could run. It never passes a move past the real end of travel. The WorkBee's owner must confirm his frame size and his real X/Y/Z travel before the values are final. The file name `ooznest-workbee-1000x1500.mch` names the frame, so it stays.\n\n## Why no post is named\n\nEstlcam publishes its rules for programs from other CAM programs (https://www.estlcam.de/steuerung_cnc_programme.php). Each motion line must have its own G word. Arcs use I/J only, with no full circles. The control ignores other G words with no message. No built-in post is confirmed to meet these rules. A post for them changes posted G-code and is under the safety floor. The follow-up is #3735 (`effort:high`).\n\n## Sources (read 2026-11-23)\n\n- https://ooznest.co.uk/product/black-1000x1500mm-workbee-z1-cnc-router-machine-ethernet-uk-power/ (working area 770x1270, Z 88, max feed 2500 mm/min, lead screw drive)\n- https://ooznest.co.uk/product-category/self-build-solutions/workbee-cnc-machine/workbee-machines/\n- https://www.estlcam.de/steuerung_cnc_programme.php\n- https://www.estlcam.de/steuerung_hardware.php and https://www.estlcam.de/hardware.php\n- The issue comments for the owner's frame, drive, work area and spindle (not public).\n\n## Tests (final head)\n\n- Pinning test: `ooznest_workbee_states_the_smaller_envelope_and_feed` (`crates/app/tests/machine_library.rs`).\n- `every_shipped_machine_mounts_and_speaks_its_declaration` (`machine.rs`) lists the new machine.\n- `every_shipped_machine_lists_and_validates_clean`, `every_machine_file_in_assets_is_in_the_library` and `every_shipped_machine_stays_standard` read it.\n- `cargo test -j 6 -p camcraft-app --test machine --test machine_library --test axis_direction`: 17, 12 and 33 passed.\n- `cargo clippy -j 6 -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No post was run against the machine. No post is named. The posted G-code of each existing machine does not change.\n- No heavy lane and no light lane were run.\n\nChangelog: New library machine \"Ooznest WorkBee 1000x1500 (Estlcam)\": X 1200, Y 770, Z 88 mm, the smaller of the owner's and Ooznest's published travel; the owner must confirm the travel, and no post is named until the Estlcam post (#3735) ships.\n\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #3038\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n",
